APX.md = {"country":{"name":"Moldova","tagline":"The most vine-covered country on earth, where a Soviet wine factory became a nation of underground cities and Fetească.","classification":"Moldova's wine law follows the EU model. At the top are wines with a protected designation of origin (Vin cu Denumire de Origine Protejată, DOP): historic appellations such as Ciumai and Romănești were already protected in the EU before 2016, but PDOs are few and little used on labels. The workhorse is the protected geographical indication (Indicație Geografică Protejată, IGP): Codru in the centre, Ștefan Vodă in the south-east and Valul lui Traian in the south-west, each managed by a growers' association that sets yields, varieties and controls. Divin is a national IGP for wine brandy aged at least three years in oak. Below these sit varietal wines and plain wine.\n\nOlder Soviet-era names survive on labels and in cellars: 'Cahor' (a sweet, fortified red in the Russian Orthodox church style, now often called Ciumai or Moldavian dessert wine), 'Negru de Purcari' and 'Roșu de Purcari' (brand names of historic blends) and 'Codru' as a red blend name. Wines labelled IGP must come from registered vineyards in the zone, and the ONVV runs a national vine and wine register."},"regions":[{"name":"Codru","slug":"codru","tagline":"Forested central hills, underground cities and Moldova's whites and sparkling wines.","ids":["md-codru","md-divin","md-romanesti"]},{"name":"Ștefan Vodă","slug":"tefan-vod","tagline":"The Dniester's last hills before the Black Sea: Purcari and the great reds.","ids":["md-stefan-voda"]},{"name":"Valul lui Traian","slug":"valul-lui-traian","tagline":"The warm south, named after a Roman earthwork, with Ciumai's dessert wines.","ids":["md-ciumai","md-valul-lui-traian"]}],"items":{"md-ciumai":{"name":"Ciumai","cat":"PDO","region":"Valul lui Traian","created":"Protected in the EU before 2016","styles":["sweet","fortified","red"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon (traditionally)","summary":"A historic appellation from the village of Ciumai in the Taraclia district, known for a deep red dessert wine in the 'Cahor' style once supplied to the Russian Orthodox church. The name was one of Moldova's first designations of origin protected in the EU.","rslug":"valul-lui-traian"},"md-codru":{"name":"Codru","cat":"IGP","region":"Codru","created":"Protected in the EU 2016","styles":["white","red","sparkling"],"grapes":"Fetească Albă, Fetească Regală, Viorica, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Aligoté, Pinot Noir, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot and others","summary":"Moldova's central IGP and its biggest, covering the forested hills around Chișinău. Cool for Moldova, it is the home of the country's fresh whites and its sparkling wine industry (Cricova, Asconi, Château Vartely, Carpe Diem, Gitana), and of the underground cellars of Cricova and Mileștii Mici. Codru reds are lighter and more aromatic than those of the south.","terroir":"Wooded hills of 200 to 400 metres on grey forest soils and chernozem over limestone; the forests keep humidity higher and nights cooler.","producers":["Cricova","Château Vartely","Asconi","Château Cojușna","Carpe Diem","Gitana","Mileștii Mici"],"nerd_note":"Wine of Moldova counted about 61,200 ha of vineyard in IGP Codru, more than half the country's wine-grape area.","rslug":"codru"},"md-divin":{"name":"Divin","cat":"IGP","region":"Codru","created":"Protected in the EU 2016","styles":["fortified"],"grapes":"Wine distillate from Moldovan grapes","summary":"A geographical indication for Moldovan wine brandy, covering the whole country. Divin must be double-distilled from wine and aged at least three years in oak; it replaced the Soviet-era name 'cognac'. Leading houses include Kvint (Tiraspol), Călărași Divin and Barza Albă.","nerd_note":"Divin covers the whole territory, including Transnistria, where the Kvint distillery has made brandy since 1897.","rslug":"codru"},"md-romanesti":{"name":"Romănești","cat":"PDO","region":"Codru","created":"Protected in the EU before 2016","styles":["red"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Malbec (Bordeaux varieties)","summary":"The historic estate and village of Romănești in the Strășeni district, Codru, whose Bordeaux-style reds were made for the imperial and later Soviet elite. Romănești was among Moldova's first designations of origin protected in the EU.","rslug":"codru"},"md-stefan-voda":{"name":"Ștefan Vodă","cat":"IGP","region":"Ștefan Vodă","created":"Protected in the EU 2016","styles":["red","rose","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Rară Neagră, Fetească Neagră, Saperavi, Malbec, Chardonnay and others","summary":"The south-eastern IGP on the lower Dniester, named after Stephen the Great, and the source of Moldova's most celebrated reds. Purcari's Negru de Purcari (Cabernet Sauvignon, Saperavi and Rară Neagră) has been made here since the nineteenth century; Et Cetera at Crocmaz and estates around Tănătari and Căușeni carry the tradition forward.","terroir":"Low slopes of 100 to 200 metres within about 60 kilometres of the Black Sea; Dniester fog and sea breezes temper winter cold and summer heat on calcareous chernozem.","producers":["Purcari","Et Cetera","Crama Mircesti"],"nerd_note":"The Purcari vineyards are about 500 metres from the Dniester and less than 2 kilometres from the Ukrainian border.","rslug":"tefan-vod"},"md-valul-lui-traian":{"name":"Valul lui Traian","cat":"IGP","region":"Valul lui Traian","created":"Protected in the EU 2016","styles":["red","white","sweet","fortified"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Fetească Neagră, Saperavi, Pinot Noir, Muscat, Chardonnay and others","summary":"The southern IGP, named after the Roman-era earthworks known as Trajan's Wall, is the warmest and driest part of Moldova. Reds make up about 60 percent of its plantings and ripen fully; it also keeps the dessert-wine traditions of Ciumai and Tomai. Large wineries in Gagauzia and around Cahul make much of the volume.","terroir":"Rolling plateaus of 100 to 250 metres, chernozem on loess, hot summers with drought risk.","producers":["Bostavan (Purcari Wineries)","Fautor","Vinăria Ciumai"],"nerd_note":"About 43,200 ha of vineyard lie in this IGP.","rslug":"valul-lui-traian"}}};
